{"title":"1995 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following operations has the same effect on a number as multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa608ff4fd7754c4ff82a2e8ac12c2fbf6ab80f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and then dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/d/31d71d52b7d9d439251ed88081bd1a8aaa5cbc6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887acab535699f80f12c552add7d2ef79a0a1391.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\text{dividing by }\\dfrac{4}{3} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\text{dividing by }\\dfrac{9}{20} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\text{multiplying by }\\dfrac{9}{20} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\text{dividing by }\\dfrac{5}{4} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\text{multiplying by }\\dfrac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"852\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac40ce1434cda0943c408cc185f5976212d95801.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae6ca439f90be5b87b92cab8cfd6ea9e3f23475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Multiplying a number by two numbers is the same as multiplying the number by the product of those two numbers.  Thus, multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae6ca439f90be5b87b92cab8cfd6ea9e3f23475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> is the same as multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/e/8def76a884afe5b2462afa898e9c620f04c13c5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3\\cdot 5}{4\\cdot 3} = \\frac{5}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"38\" />, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55206bce678ac0394d97dc04dd72398df2bdf572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME\" title=\"1995 AJHSME\">1995 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/i